Android companion to patches/ui-patches/neterror-common.patch (LW-M1-07).

The common half repoints NET_ERROR_ILLUSTRATIONS.securityError at
chrome://global/skin/illustrations/warning.svg and adds the SVG under
toolkit/themes/shared/illustrations/. On desktop that file is packaged by
toolkit/themes/shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn, which the desktop half edits.
toolkit/themes/moz.build:19-26 routes MOZ_BUILD_APP == "mobile/android" to
toolkit/themes/mobile, whose only manifest (toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn)
includes shared/minimal-toolkit.jar.inc.mn and never desktop-jar.inc.mn, so
nothing would package the illustration for Android.

The reference is not reachable on Android today - see the LW-M1-07 finding:
NetErrorCard.isSupported() short-circuits on security.certerrors.felt-privacy-v1,
which is set only in browser/app/profile/firefox.js, and Fenix's
AppRequestInterceptor.onErrorRequest replaces every load error with its own page.
This entry exists so that the reference cannot become a silent 404 the moment any
of that changes. It costs one 600-byte SVG in the APK.

Note the illustration is added to the mobile-only manifest, NOT to
shared/minimal-toolkit.jar.inc.mn: desktop-jar.inc.mn:10 includes
minimal-toolkit.jar.inc.mn, so an entry there would also land in the desktop jar
and break the byte-identical-desktop-tree guarantee.

160 rebase (2026-11-11, Firefox 160.0): jar.mn gained aboutLicense.css and,
at its end, the Android picture-in-picture entries
(picture-in-picture-open-android.svg, pictureinpicture/texttracks.css). The
same illustration entry is appended at the new end of the file; only the hunk's
context and position changed.

diff --git a/toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn b/toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn
index 11df690..f703347 100644
--- a/toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn
+++ b/toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn
@@ -14,3 +14,8 @@
    skin/classic/global/media/picture-in-picture-open-android.svg (../../shared/media/picture-in-picture-open-android.svg)
 #  picture-in-picture, for the caption overlay in the player window:
    skin/classic/global/pictureinpicture/texttracks.css      (../../shared/pictureinpicture/texttracks.css)
+
+# LibreWolf: illustration used by the net error card
+# (toolkit/content/errors/net-error-illustrations.mjs). Desktop gets it from
+# shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn, which this manifest does not include.
+  skin/classic/global/illustrations/warning.svg            (../../shared/illustrations/warning.svg)
